---
import PlaygroundShell from '../../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
---
<PlaygroundShell title="Training set vs what serving saw" hint="Each of 500 labels is joined with a 'purchases so far' feature. The check: does the training value equal the value the online store held at that moment? The dataset is 20 users and 622 purchases over 1,000 minutes.">
  <ol class="how">
    <li>The default is the <b>event-time as-of join</b> with a <b>10-minute</b> pipeline delay: it looks right, and is wrong for <b>141 of 500</b> labels, because the join used purchases that had happened but not yet reached the online store.</li>
    <li>Choose <b>latest value</b>: wrong for almost every label (<b>486 of 500</b> at 10 minutes), because the future leaks in. Slide the delay to 0 and the event-time join becomes exact, but latest stays wrong.</li>
    <li>Choose <b>as-of the time the value was available</b>: exact at every delay (0 of 500). The row's available time is its event time plus the delay.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="pg fsb" data-fsb>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Training join <select class="pg-in" data-j>
        <option value="latest">latest value of the user</option>
        <option value="event" selected>as of the label time, by event time</option>
        <option value="avail">as of the label time, by time available</option>
      </select></label>
      <label>Pipeline delay (minutes) <input type="range" min="0" max="30" value="10" data-lag /> <b data-lagval></b></label>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-grid">
      <div class="pg-box" data-b1><h3>Labels with the wrong value</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o1></span><span class="pg-note" data-n1></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b2><h3>Average error when wrong</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o2></span><span class="pg-note" data-n2></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b3><h3>Example label</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o3></span><span class="pg-note" data-n3></span></div>
    </div>
    <p class="pg-out" data-verdict aria-live="polite"></p>
    <p class="pg-note">Model: purchases arrive about every 30 minutes per user, at random. The correct training value is what the online store held at the label time: purchases whose event time plus the pipeline delay is at or before it. The error is the number of purchases the training value is off by.</p>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<script>
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-fsb]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = <T extends HTMLElement>(s: string) => root.querySelector<T>(s)!;
    const USERS = 20; const SPAN = 1000; const LABELS = 500;
    const SEED = 11; const MEAN_GAP = 30; const LABEL_START = 100; // mean time between a user's events; labels only after t=100
    let seed = SEED; const rnd = () => ((seed = (seed * 1664525 + 1013904223) % 4294967296) / 4294967296);
    const ev: number[][] = [];
    for (let u = 0; u < USERS; u++) { const a: number[] = []; let t = 0; for (;;) { t += Math.floor(-Math.log(1 - rnd()) * MEAN_GAP) + 1; if (t > SPAN) break; a.push(t); } ev.push(a); }
    const labels = Array.from({ length: LABELS }, () => ({ u: Math.floor(rnd() * USERS), t: LABEL_START + Math.floor(rnd() * (SPAN - LABEL_START)) }));
    function draw() {
      const join = q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-j]').value; const lag = Number(q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-lag]').value);
      q('[data-lagval]').textContent = String(lag);
      let wrong = 0; let off = 0; let example = '';
      labels.forEach((l) => {
        const a = ev[l.u];
        const served = a.filter((t) => t + lag <= l.t).length;
        const got = join === 'latest' ? a.length : join === 'event' ? a.filter((t) => t <= l.t).length : served;
        if (got !== served) { wrong++; off += Math.abs(got - served); if (!example) example = `user ${l.u} at minute ${l.t}: training value ${got}, online store held ${served}`; }
      });
      q('[data-o1]').textContent = `${wrong} of ${LABELS}`; q('[data-n1]').textContent = `${Math.round((wrong / LABELS) * 100)}% of the training examples disagree with serving`;
      q('[data-o2]').textContent = wrong ? `${(off / wrong).toFixed(1)} purchases` : 'none'; q('[data-n2]').textContent = wrong ? 'larger means a more misleading feature' : 'no label is wrong';
      q('[data-o3]').textContent = example || 'all labels agree'; q('[data-n3]').textContent = example ? 'the first label that disagrees' : 'training equals serving';
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-b1]').style.setProperty('--c', wrong ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--good)');
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-b2]').style.setProperty('--c', 'var(--accent)');
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-b3]').style.setProperty('--c', 'var(--accent)');
      const out = q('[data-verdict]'); out.classList.toggle('bad', wrong > 0);
      out.textContent = wrong === 0 ? (join === 'latest' ? 'No label disagrees.' : `Training matches serving on all ${LABELS} labels. The join used only values that were already available at the label time.`)
        : join === 'latest' ? `Wrong on ${wrong} of ${LABELS}: the newest value includes purchases made after the label, so the model learns from the future and offline scores look better than production.`
        : `Wrong on ${wrong} of ${LABELS}: the join counted purchases that had happened but were still in the pipeline for up to ${lag} minutes, so serving never saw them. Join by the time the value was available.`;
    }
    root.addEventListener('input', draw); root.addEventListener('change', draw);
    draw();
  });
</script>
